---
code: K0016
title: Pipe Target Not Call
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, pipe, operator, call]
description: "Right-hand side of '|>' must be a call or contain a '_' placeholder"
---

The right-hand stage of a forward pipe (`|>`) must either be a function or variant call (`f(y)` or `Variant()`)—into which the piped value is inserted as the first argument—or an expression containing a `_` placeholder. Bare function names, operators without `_`, or literals are not valid pipe targets.

## Example

This error occurs when piping into a bare function identifier without parentheses or into an expression that lacks a `_` placeholder:

```kura
let a = 10 |> increment

let b = 10 |> 1 + 2
```

## Solution

Call the target function with `()`, or use `_` to mark where the piped value should be substituted:

```kura
let a = 10 |> increment()

let b = 10 |> add(_, 20)
let c = 10 |> _ + 2
```
